</ul>
<p>None of them fit a job that shows up every morning and takes five minutes.</p>

<h2 id="broom-mistake">The biggest mistake people make about the broom</h2>
<p>Most of us grew up thinking the broom is the gentle, easy choice. It isn't. It's the slowest tool on the porch, and it doesn't finish the job.</p>
<p>A broom only pushes. The big pieces move. The fine stuff, the grit and needle bits and pollen, drops into the cracks and the grain of the wood. It looks clean. By noon, it isn't.</p>
<p>One buyer of the blower in this story found that out in the garage:</p>
